  "limitations": "Seven reviewed value sets, not all style fields. Grid minima need explicit track counts for GPUIX-equivalent behavior. Decoration maps user intent; GPUIO explicitly replaces both decorations, including inherited values. See finite-value evidence for these differences. Gradient has paired encoding, native validation/GPU and public gallery evidence. Cursor/overflow mapping and focused gallery evidence do not establish physical OS cursor glyphs or Linux desktop acceptance. Full combined gallery/consumer and release gates remain."
